      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:6:8:1:7",
      "text": [
        " رَآنِي أَبُو عَبْدِ اللَّهِ ( عليه السلام ) وَ أَنَا أَحْمِلُ بَقْلًا فَقَالَ يُكْرَهُ لِلرَّجُلِ السَّرِيِّ أَنْ يَحْمِلَ الشَّيْ‏ءَ الدَّنِيَّ فَيُجْتَرَأَ عَلَيْهِ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Ali Bin Ibrahim, from his father, from Ibn Abu Umeyr, from one of his companions, from Muawiya Bin Wahab who said, ",
          "‘Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup> saw me and I was carrying grass. So he<sup>asws</sup> said: ‘It is disliked for the man of magnanimity that he should be carrying the lowly thing so they (people) would be audacious (disrespectful) towards him’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "7. Ali ibn Ibrahim has narrated from his father from ibn abu ‘Umayr from certain persons of his people from Mu‘awiyah ibn Wahab who has said the following: “Abu ‘Abd Allah, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, once saw me carrying grass. He (the Imam) said, ‘It is undesirable for a man of dignity to carry lowly things, thus people become bold against him.’” "
        ]
      }
    },
